# html.rs — native HTML for the desktop

A Rust framework for native cross-platform desktop apps (macOS/Windows/Linux) **and web**,
built directly on `winit` + `wgpu`. **No webview, no Wry/CEF, no JS engine** — the `ui!`
macro compiles HTML-like markup into an element tree that a custom wgpu renderer paints.
Reactivity is state-based (like modern JS frameworks), not VDOM-diffing.

## Crate map

| Crate | Role |
|---|---|
| `crates/html_rs_state` | Fine-grained reactive state (`State<T>` is `Copy`), effects, memos, `batch`, `untrack`. Thread-local runtime, single-threaded by design. |
| `crates/html_rs_core` | `Element`/`Node`/`TextNode` tree, event types (`PointerEvent`, `KeyEventInfo`, handler constructors `click`/`input`/`enter`/`key`), the **Tailwind class compiler** (`style.rs` → taffy `Style` + paint props; `colors.rs` → Tailwind palette; `tag_default_classes` gives semantic tags browser-style default classes), and the **tree diff engine** (`diff.rs` → `diff_element`/`equivalent`). |
| `crates/html_rs_macro` | The `ui!` proc macro: hand-rolled HTML parser over `proc_macro::TokenTree` (no syn/quote). |
| `crates/html_rs_render` | The renderer: taffy flexbox layout → SDF rounded-rect quads (WGSL, `shader.wgsl`), a textured pass for decoded `<img>` files (`image.wgsl`), and glyphon/cosmic-text for text. |
| root crate `html_rs` | Facade: re-exports everything + `runtime.rs` (winit `ApplicationHandler`, `launch()`) . |

Dependency direction: `macro → (nothing)`, `core → taffy`, `render → core, wgpu, glyphon, taffy`, root → all.

## Render pipeline (every repaint)

1. A state write flushes queued effects → the single **render effect** in `runtime.rs`
   re-invokes the user's view closure. If the new `Element` tree is
   `html_rs_core::equivalent` to the stored one, the repaint is **skipped**;
   otherwise the new tree replaces `Shared.tree`.
2. `RedrawRequested` → `Renderer::paint` (incremental via `PaintState` in `painter.rs`):
   - diff the new tree against the previous frame's item list, positionally:
     unchanged subtrees reuse their taffy nodes (skipped by taffy's layout cache);
     class/content changes patch the existing node (`set_style` / `set_node_context`);
     structural changes tear down the old taffy nodes and build that subtree fresh;
   - `compute_layout_with_measure` runs flexbox — only dirty subtrees re-layout;
     text leaves are measured by cosmic-text shaping (shaped `Rc<Buffer>`s are
     cached per item and reused while content/size/wrap are unchanged),
   - walk the flat item list (preorder) emitting `Quad`s, shaped `TextItem`s and
     `HitTarget`s (hit testing is "topmost last wins", z-order = tree order).
3. `Renderer::render`: upload **only changed quad-instance ranges** (diff vs previous
   frame) → glyphon `prepare` text → one render pass (clear → instanced quads →
   text) → present.
4. Window resize or scale-factor change resets `PaintState` (full rebuild); steady-
   state frames are incremental.

## Coordinate spaces (important)

- Layout/paint/hit-testing run in **physical pixels** (class px values are multiplied by
  the window `scale_factor` at parse time).
- `PointerEvent` coordinates passed to handlers are **logical** CSS pixels.
- Colors in `html_rs_core` are **sRGB floats**; the GPU expects **linear** (targets are
  `*UnormSrgb`) — always convert with `srgb_to_linear` when building quads.

## Conventions

- All framework types are re-exported from the root crate: `html_rs::{ui, launch, State, Element, ...}`.
  The macro generates `::html_rs::...` paths, so keep those re-exports intact.
- Unknown Tailwind classes are silently ignored; known ones live in `core/src/style.rs`.
- Examples live in `examples/*.rs` and are registered as `[[bin]]` targets
  (`autoexamples = false` — bins are what Trunk builds for wasm). Run them with
  `cargo run --bin 01_hello_world`.
